# Grid B — U1 Security audit (path traversal in REPL → filesystem)
#
# Gap target: taint-tracking through REPL input → file operations
# without a dedicated security scenario. This case is deliberately
# adversarial: the answer should name specific code paths where
# user-controlled strings reach filesystem APIs, not abstract advice.
#
# Ground truth: ordinary chat/request text is only pipeline content,
# and store paths such as log_dir / memory_dir are resolved from CLI
# flags / YAML at boot time. REPL attachment commands are different:
# `/log <path>`, `/log append <path>`, `/htrace <path>`, and
# `/htrace append <path>` intentionally read the operator-supplied
# path with os.ReadFile. A grounded answer should either name those
# direct read surfaces with file:line anchors or explain why another
# alleged surface is bounded by store-ID validation / directory
# enumeration.
ID="u1b"
NAME="security audit — REPL input reaching filesystem operations"
QUESTION="Which code paths in internal/repl pass raw user input into a filesystem operation (open / write / mkdir) without sanitization? Name the files and line ranges."
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC was just `repl` — the
# question's path token; bar = "复述题目". Tighten by requiring the
# answer to either name the FS-API surface (read|open|write|mkdir from
# the question itself) AND a specific repl file (commands.go or
# session.go are likely sites — answer must verify path lineage,
# not just claim no risk). Negative gates already block the
# stereotype brush-off.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="repl"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="internal/repl/[a-z_]+\.go
(read|open|write|mkdir|os\.ReadFile|os\.Create|os\.Open|os\.MkdirAll|filepath\.Join)"
# 2026-05-08: previous EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="assumed stereotype generally
# no risk" tokenised on whitespace, banning the single-character substring
# "no" — which case-insensitively matches "Note", "node", "no risk
# identified", and many innocent words. Model answer (correctly identified
# baselineShow at handle_baseline.go:137 as the unprotected path AND
# enumerated 5 sanitised peers) failed solely because the diagram had
# "Note over hb" labels. Drop the gate — the three positive gates above
# (repl identifier + internal/repl/<file>.go regex + FS-API regex)
# already block brush-off "no risk" answers: such answers cannot satisfy
# the FS-API regex without naming a real file:line.
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS=""
